  "scope": "Ordinary and audited cancellation entry coordination moves to the product adapter. Native owners retain expiration/reconciliation, group visibility, journal identity/idempotency checks, transactions and commit-before-publication.",
  "limitations": [
    "Trusted Leserpent product policy, not raw ingress or the standalone generic VM. Metadata validity and matching local images do not grant authority; input bounds, provenance, debugger authority and trusted time remain caller obligations.",
    "Callbacks execute once without retry or rollback. Native transactions retain their own rollback boundaries, and group visibility can fail after a cancellation has committed.",
    "The oracle freezes the complete prior entry coordinators and shares metadata validators, state machinery and journals. It proves coordinator compatibility, not independent implementation of those lower layers.",
    "Retry coordination, native result conversion/settlement, journal ownership, complete host-neutral durable recovery, vertical compatibility and physical extraction remain open. Native completion and maturity are unchanged.",
    "Local macOS Rust/SQLite verification only; no Linux, GUI or remote CI run. The existing 280-file standalone checkpoint was integrity-checked, not freshly exported or retested."
  ],
